    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is grease interceptor cleaning?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Grease interceptor cleaning involves professional removal of accumulated fats, oils, and grease from grease interceptors or grease traps in commercial food establishments. Process includes thorough emptying and cleaning using specialized equipment like hydro-jetting systems, inspection, repairs if needed, proper documentation, and resealing."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why is grease interceptor cleaning important?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Grease interceptor cleaning important because accumulated fats, oils, and grease can cause blockages in plumbing systems and municipal sewer lines. Regular cleaning maintains system functionality, prevents costly repairs, protects environment, ensures compliance with health department requirements, and helps businesses avoid penalties and closure."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How often do grease interceptors need cleaning?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Grease interceptors need cleaning at least annually recommended by professionals, though more frequent cleaning every three months or even monthly may be necessary depending on system size, volume of grease-producing activities, local regulations, and compliance requirements specific to Miami-Dade County area."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does grease interceptor cleaning involve?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Professional grease interceptor cleaning involves thorough emptying and cleaning using line-jetting technology and hydro-jetting systems using high-pressure water to remove stubborn grease buildup, inspection and assessment to identify damage, repairs addressing broken components, proper documentation and compliance records, and resealing and deodorizing service area."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are regulations for grease interceptor maintenance?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Miami-Dade County has specific regulatory requirements for grease trap maintenance that commercial food establishments must follow. Professional service providers handle FOG compliance issues ensuring all necessary documentation completed. Licensed companies provide inspections, repairs, and certifications. Businesses required to maintain records of grease trap service to avoid violations."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are benefits of professional cleaning?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Professional cleaning benefits include prevention of blockages maintaining system efficiency, compliance with Miami-Dade health regulations preventing violations and fines, protection of municipal sewer systems preventing environmental contamination, prevention of costly repairs and operational disruptions, proper documentation ensuring regulatory compliance, and same-day emergency service availability."
