      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "While not required by law, maintenance plans are highly recommended for all septic systems, especially older systems, high-usage properties, properties preparing for sale, and systems in high water table areas. Even newer systems benefit from regular professional oversight."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does preventive septic maintenance include?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Preventive maintenance includes regular inspections, scheduled pumping, filter cleaning and replacement, minor component repairs, drainfield condition monitoring, compliance verification, and documentation of all work performed. The goal is preventing problems before they become expensive failures."
      }
