        "text": "Lift station monitoring and service in Miami typically costs $200-$500 per month for monitoring services plus maintenance costs depending on service frequency, system complexity, monitoring technology, and maintenance scope. Basic monthly monitoring costs $200-$350. Comprehensive service agreements cost $400-$800+ per month."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is lift station monitoring and service?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Lift station monitoring and service involves use of electronic devices (RTU Remote Terminal Units) and professional technicians to control, monitor, and maintain lift stations remotely and on-site, providing constant system visibility enabling operators to respond quickly to issues and minimize downtime while ensuring reliable operation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why is lift station monitoring important?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Lift station monitoring important because failures can lead to serious consequences including sewerage backups, property damage, environmental hazards, flooding, and health risks. Remote monitoring systems provide constant system visibility enabling operators to respond quickly to issues and minimize downtime preventing costly repairs."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does lift station monitoring include?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Lift station monitoring includes pump control and status monitoring, alarm monitoring detecting system malfunctions, data acquisition collecting real-time operational data, communication transmitting status information remotely, system diagnostics providing comprehensive analysis, and level alarms monitoring wastewater levels. Advanced systems utilize satellite communications for backup monitoring during power outages."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How often do lift stations need service?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Lift stations need service monthly for alarm testing, quarterly for float switch checks, semi-annually for wet well cleaning and pump inspection, and annually for complete system inspections and testing of backflow preventers. Miami-Dade County requires compliance with county-specific RTU monitoring and maintenance requirements."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are common lift station problems?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Common lift station problems include alarms going off or failing to activate, overflow or sewage backup near lift station, loud noises or vibrations from pumps, persistent sewer odors, and water level not dropping after pump cycles. These indicate pump failures, electrical issues, or control malfunctions requiring professional attention."
      }
    },
