        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Systems typically need annual inspections and pumping every 2-3 years for average households. Frequency depends on household size, water usage, tank size, system age, and Miami's environmental conditions. Professional contractors evaluate your specific system and recommend appropriate service frequency."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the difference between contract and one-time service?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Contracts provide scheduled preventive maintenance with predictable costs, priority scheduling, and discounts. One-time services provide individual service when needed with no ongoing commitment but may cost more over time and don't include preventive care. Contracts prevent problems; one-time services address problems after they occur."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens if I cancel a septic service contract?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Cancellation terms vary by provider. Some require 30-60 days notice. Early cancellation fees may apply. You receive service until cancellation date but lose priority scheduling and discounts after. Review contract terms carefully before signing to understand cancellation policies."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I get a service contract for an older septic system?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, contracts are available for older systems and may be especially valuable for maintaining aging equipment. Older systems may benefit from more frequent service. Contracts provide regular care that extends life of older systems. Professional evaluation determines appropriate service frequency."
      }
    }
  ]
}

