{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is septic tank sludge?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Septic tank sludge is the layer of settled solid waste that accumulates at the bottom of septic tanks. Heavier solids settle due to gravity, forming sludge layer over time. When sludge reaches one-third of tank depth, removal is needed to prevent system problems and protect drain fields from damage."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does septic sludge removal cost?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Sludge and scum removal typically costs $400-$800 in Miami-Dade County. Small tanks cost $300-$500. Standard tanks cost $400-$700. Large tanks cost $600-$1,200. Costs vary based on tank size, layer thickness, and equipment needed."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How often should sludge be removed from septic tank?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Sludge and scum removal should be done every 3-5 years as part of routine maintenance, or when layers become excessive. When sludge reaches one-third of tank depth, removal is needed immediately. Regular removal prevents layers from reaching critical levels that cause system problems."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the difference between pumping and sludge removal?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Regular pumping removes liquid and some sludge but doesn't completely clean tank interior. Complete removal thoroughly cleans all layers and tank interior, using specialized equipment like pressure washing to break up hardened materials. Removal costs more ($400-$800) than pumping ($200-$400) but provides thorough cleaning when layers are excessive."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I remove sludge from my septic tank myself?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Professional removal is strongly recommended because it requires specialized equipment, proper disposal methods, and knowledge of tank safety. DIY removal is dangerous due to toxic gases and improper disposal issues. Professionals have equipment to break up hardened sludge and ensure proper disposal following regulations."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens if sludge is not removed?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "If sludge is not removed, it continues accumulating until reaching critical levels that cause system problems. Excessive sludge reduces tank capacity, allows solids to enter drain fields causing damage, causes backups into home, leads to drain field failure requiring expensive replacement, and creates health hazards from system malfunction."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does sludge and scum removal take?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
